  "organization": "ScaleDock",
  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers the Universal Commerce Protocol (UCP) for agentic commerce with five version lines: UCP 2026-08-25 (current, release branch at 3a541e13), UCP 2026-04-08 (supported, still receiving backports), UCP 2026-01-23 and UCP 2026-01-11 (legacy, upgrade from), and the UCP draft on ucp.dev (preview, posture track). It teaches business and platform profiles, reverse-domain naming and schema authority binding, version selection and exact-version capability negotiation, the REST, MCP, A2A and Embedded transports, the checkout lifecycle with fulfillment and discount, payment handlers, credentials, AP2 mandates and 3DS authentication, identity linking over OAuth 2.0, orders with signed webhooks, and RFC 9421 message signatures. References cover version lines and upgrades, discovery and negotiation, checkout, payments, and identity and orders.",
